---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "@components/Hero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Attorney Assistant's privacy policy. Learn what personal information we collect, how we use it, how we share it, and our SMS messaging disclosures.">

  <Hero
    title="Privacy Policy"
    subtitle="Last updated: May 2026"
    size="sm"
  />

  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <div class="prose-brand">
        <h2>Introduction</h2>
        <p>
          Attorney Assistant ("we," "our," or "us") is committed to protecting your privacy.
          This Privacy Policy explains what personal information we collect, how we collect it,
          how we use it, and the limited circumstances under which we share it when you visit our
          website (attorneyassistant.com) or use our services.
        </p>
        <p>
          By using our website or services, you agree to the practices described in this Privacy Policy.
        </p>

        <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

        <h3>Personal Information You Provide</h3>
        <p>
          We collect personal information that you voluntarily provide to us when you fill out a form,
          schedule a consultation, subscribe to communications, request resources, or otherwise interact
          with our website or team. This may include:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your name (first and last)</li>
          <li>Email address</li>
          <li>Phone number (mobile and/or office)</li>
          <li>Firm or company name, role, and professional details (such as practice area, firm size, lead volume, or operational metrics you choose to share in a self-assessment)</li>
          <li>Mailing address (when you provide it)</li>
          <li>Information you submit in free-text fields, such as questions, comments, or details about your firm's needs</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>SMS / Text Messaging Information</h3>
        <p>
          If you choose to opt in to receive text messages from us, we collect your mobile phone number
          and your SMS consent record (timestamp, opt-in source, and the message you consented to receive).
        </p>

        <h3>Information Collected Automatically</h3>
        <p>When you visit our website, we and our service providers automatically collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Browser type, version, and language</li>
          <li>Operating system and device type</li>
          <li>IP address and approximate geographic location (city/region level)</li>
          <li>Pages visited, time spent on each page, and referring website</li>
          <li>Cookies, pixel tags, and similar tracking technologies (see "Cookies & Tracking" below)</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Information from Third-Party Sources</h3>
        <p>
          We may receive limited information about you from third parties such as analytics providers,
          advertising platforms (e.g., Meta, LinkedIn, Google), or referral partners. This information
          is used to measure the performance of our marketing and to improve your experience on our site.
        </p>

        <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Provide, operate, and improve our services and website</li>
          <li>Respond to your inquiries, schedule consultations, and provide customer support</li>
          <li>Send you transactional messages (e.g., appointment reminders, account or service updates, follow-ups to a request you initiated)</li>
          <li>Send you marketing and informational communications about our services, where permitted (you may opt out at any time)</li>
          <li>Send you SMS messages if you have opted in</li>
          <li>Analyze website usage and improve content, performance, and user experience</li>
          <li>Measure the effectiveness of our advertising and marketing campaigns</li>
          <li>Prevent fraud, abuse, and security incidents, and enforce our terms</li>
          <li>Comply with applicable laws, regulations, and legal process</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How We Share Your Information</h2>
        <p>
          We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information. We share personal information only
          in the limited circumstances described below.
        </p>

        <h3 id="sms-no-sharing">SMS Consent and Phone Numbers — Not Shared</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>
            We do not share, sell, rent, or otherwise disclose your SMS opt-in consent or your mobile
            phone number to any third parties or affiliates for their own marketing purposes.
            SMS consent and phone numbers collected for the purpose of SMS communications are used solely
            by Attorney Assistant to deliver the messages you have consented to receive.
          </strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          The only exception is that we may transmit your mobile number to the SMS service providers
          and telecommunications carriers strictly as needed to deliver messages to you, and to comply
          with applicable laws. These providers are contractually prohibited from using your number or
          consent for any other purpose.
        </p>

        <h3>Service Providers</h3>
        <p>
          We share personal information with vendors and service providers that help us operate our
          business, including (without limitation): website hosting, CRM and email delivery, analytics,
          advertising measurement, scheduling, payment processing, and customer support tools. These
          providers are authorized to use your information only to perform services on our behalf.
        </p>

        <h3>Legal and Safety Disclosures</h3>
        <p>
          We may disclose personal information when we believe in good faith that disclosure is necessary
          to (a) comply with a legal obligation, subpoena, or government request; (b) protect and defend
          our rights or property; (c) prevent or investigate possible wrongdoing; (d) protect the personal
          safety of users or the public; or (e) protect against legal liability.
        </p>

        <h3>Business Transfers</h3>
        <p>
          If we are involved in a merger, acquisition, financing, reorganization, or sale of assets,
          personal information may be transferred as part of that transaction, subject to standard
          confidentiality protections.
        </p>

        <h3>With Your Consent</h3>
        <p>
          We may share personal information for any other purpose with your consent or at your direction.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies & Tracking Technologies</h2>
        <p>
          We use cookies, pixels, and similar technologies to operate our website, remember your preferences,
          analyze site usage, and measure advertising. These include first-party cookies as well as
          third-party services such as Google Tag Manager / Google Analytics, Meta Pixel, LinkedIn Insight
          Tag, HubSpot, and PostHog. You can control cookies through your browser settings; disabling
          cookies may affect site functionality.
        </p>

        <h2>Data Security</h2>
        <p>
          We implement reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards designed to protect
          your personal information against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction.
          No method of transmission over the Internet or electronic storage is 100% secure, however, and
          we cannot guarantee absolute security.
        </p>

        <h2>Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
          We retain personal information for as long as needed to provide our services, comply with our
          legal obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce our agreements. When information is no longer
          needed, we securely delete or anonymize it.
        </p>

        <h2>Your Rights and Choices</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or receive a copy
          of the personal information we hold about you, and to opt out of certain processing. To exercise
          these rights, email us at
          <a href="mailto:privacy@attorneyassistant.com">privacy@attorneyassistant.com</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Opting out of marketing:</strong> You can unsubscribe from marketing emails using the
          link in any marketing email, and you can opt out of SMS at any time by replying STOP to any
          message we send.
        </p>

        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Our website and services are intended for business users and are not directed to children
          under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you
          believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us so we can delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will post the updated policy on this
          page and update the "Last updated" date above. Material changes will be communicated through
          a prominent notice on our website or by other appropriate means.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact Us</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or your personal
          information, please contact us:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Email: <a href="mailto:privacy@attorneyassistant.com">privacy@attorneyassistant.com</a></li>
          <li>Mail: Attorney Assistant, 21 East 5th Avenue, Suite 102, Conshohocken, PA 19428</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
